# Custom Robotic Arm - Essential Requirements

Status: **Confirmed** = selected requirement; **Provisional** = current design target;
**TBD/Validation required** = must be resolved before design freeze.

## 1. Architecture and scope

| Topic / item | Plan / execution description | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Configuration | Five arm joints plus one gripper DOF, using the SO-ARM101 arrangement: J1 yaw, J2/J3/J4 pitch, J5 tool roll, G1 gripper. | Confirmed |
| Axis geometry | J1/J2 intersect at the shoulder centre; J2/J3/J4 are parallel; J4/J5 intersect at the wrist centre. | Confirmed |
| Kinematic convention | Standard DH for J1-J5: `Rz(theta) Tz(d) Tx(a) Rx(alpha)`. G1 is outside the arm-pose chain. | Confirmed |
| Mounting and coordinates | Fixed upright bench mount. Origin at the J1 axis on the bench; +Z up, +X forward and +Y left. | Confirmed |
| Gripper scope | Develop the mechanical gripper first, then the pneumatic soft gripper. Preserve future modular compatibility with vacuum and electromagnetic tools. | Confirmed |

## 2. Approved hardware allocation

| Topic / item | Plan / execution description | Status |
|---|---|---|
| J1 / J3 / J4 / J5 | Each uses one Rtelligent 42AM08 NEMA 17 stepper, its appropriate driver and an external gearbox. No external encoder is used. Use 0.71 N.m for conservative sizing (manufacturer data shows 0.80 N.m typical; confirm purchased SKU). | Confirmed |
| J2 | Use StepperOnline 23HS45-3504S NEMA 23, `3.0 N.m` holding torque, `3.5 A/phase`, with an external gearbox and a separate driver rated for at least `3.5 A/phase`. | Selected provisional |
| Position reference | J1-J3 operate open-loop and require repeatable homing/limit references plus missed-step validation. | Required |
| J4-J5 | Replace the two ST3215 serial servos with one Rtelligent 42AM08 NEMA 17 stepper plus gearbox per joint. | User directed |
| G1 | Retain the third Waveshare ST3215 for the mechanical gripper. | Confirmed |
| Power | 24 V for the stepper/drive subsystem; 12 V for ST3215 servos and pneumatic hardware. | Confirmed |
| Pneumatic placement | Keep the pump and regulator off-arm wherever practical; move only lightweight tubing, valve/control hardware and the soft tool. | Confirmed approach |

